{"content":[{"c":["TAHPANHES"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Important Egyptian center in the eastern Delta. Listed with Memphis among Israel’s enemies (",{"href":"?bref=Jer.2.16","r":"Jer.2.16","rawR":"Jer.2.16","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jer.2.16","value":"Jer.2.16"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jer 2:16"},"), it is the place to which Jews fled after the murder of Gedaliah in 586 ",{"c":["BC"],"sourceClass":"era","t":"span"}," when Jeremiah was taken to Egypt (",{"href":"?bref=Jer.43.7-9","r":"Jer.43.7-9","rawR":"Jer.43.7-9","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jer.43.7-9","value":"Jer.43.7-9"}],"t":"ref","v":"43:7-9"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Jer.44.1","r":"Jer.44.1","rawR":"Jer.44.1","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jer.44.1","value":"Jer.44.1"}],"t":"ref","v":"44:1"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Jer.46.14","r":"Jer.46.14","rawR":"Jer.46.14","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jer.46.14","value":"Jer.46.14"}],"t":"ref","v":"46:14"},"). Ezekiel prophesied doom against this city (alternately spelled Tehaphnehes in ",{"href":"?bref=Ezek.30.18","r":"Ezek.30.18","rawR":"Ezek.30.18","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Ezek.30.18","value":"Ezek.30.18"}],"t":"ref","v":"Ez 30:18"},", ",{"c":["rsv"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"},")."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"},{"c":["Today the site is identified with Tell Dephneh (Defenneh), 26 miles (41.8 kilometers) southwest of Port Said. There is little evidence of occupation here before the time of Psammetichus I (664–610 ",{"c":["BC"],"sourceClass":"era","t":"span"},"), who established a fortress at the site and left a garrison of Greek mercenaries. Pharaoh’s palace in Tahpanhes, where Jeremiah buried stones as a promise of Nebuchadnezzar’s invasion (",{"href":"?bref=Jer.43.9","r":"Jer.43.9","rawR":"Jer.43.9","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Jer.43.9","value":"Jer.43.9"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jer 43:9"},"), has been identified with the fortress of Psammetichus. A fragmentary Neo-Babylonian text of the 37th year of Nebuchadnezzar refers to operations against Pharaoh Amasis and a Greek garrison."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Tahpanhes","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Jer 2:16","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Jer.2.16","rawQueryValue":"Jer.2.16","sourceRefExact":"Jer.2.16"},{"anchorText":"43:7-9","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Jer.43.7-9","rawQueryValue":"Jer.43.7-9","sourceRefExact":"Jer.43.7-9"},{"anchorText":"44:1","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Jer.44.1","rawQueryValue":"Jer.44.1","sourceRefExact":"Jer.44.1"},{"anchorText":"46:14","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Jer.46.14","rawQueryValue":"Jer.46.14","sourceRefExact":"Jer.46.14"},{"anchorText":"Ez 30:18","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Ezek.30.18","rawQueryValue":"Ezek.30.18","sourceRefExact":"Ezek.30.18"},{"anchorText":"Jer 43:9","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Jer.43.9","rawQueryValue":"Jer.43.9","sourceRefExact":"Jer.43.9"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"d79388c3d96cd6f92f016043eef0a7a8a3d8b16ccc71369d8b0de025046cab1b","sourceItemName":"Tahpanhes","sourceItemOrder":29,"sourceMember":"Articles/T.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Tahpanhes","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Tahpanhes","title":"Tahpanhes","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}